Description:
A Three-Story Residential and Commercial Building
with grounds, courtyard, rear building, and all other appurtenances, all in one plot, located in Luxembourg, 46 Avenue de la Liberté, between Jacques Biwer on one side, Dr. Gantenbein on the other, bordering Avenue de la Liberté at the front and Glesener Frères at the back, measuring 2 ares 05 centiares.   The said property, which is in very good condition, contains:
on the ground floor: large spacious commercial premises with a pastry shop salon (Konditorei-Salon), a living room, and kitchen in the side wing;
in the rear building: bakehouse in the cellar, 2 living rooms as well as a living room above them and 1 bathroom;
on the 1st floor: 4 fine living rooms, 1 kitchen, and 1 bathroom;
on the 2nd floor: 4 large living rooms, 1 kitchen, and 1 bathroom;
on the 3rd floor: 4 living rooms, 1 kitchen, and 1 bathroom.
Furthermore, 5 mansard rooms, spacious attic space, and large cellars.
Electricity, gas, W.C., mains drainage (tout-à-l'égout), and water connection.
☞ Favorable capital investment. ☜   For viewings of the property to be auctioned, please apply to the owner Mr. MAASSEN, 4 rue des Dahlias, and for information regarding the terms, apply to the undersigned notary.
Luxembourg, April 5, 1938.
Edmond REIFFERS, Notary.
